---
import SectionHeading from './SectionHeading.astro';
import Command from './Command.astro';
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import download from '../data/downloads.json';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<section id="setup" class="setup section" aria-labelledby="setup-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="setup-heading">
      <SectionHeading index="07" label="Start with the CLI" title="Your next task starts here." id="setup-title">
        <p>Python 3.10+, a local project, and a running inference worker. The setup guide takes you through each step.</p>
      </SectionHeading>
      <div class="setup-actions">
        <a class="button button-primary" href={base + 'downloads/freecompute-v1-source.zip'} download>Download source preview <Icon name="arrow" /></a>
        <a class="text-link" href={base + 'guide/'}>Open the setup guide <Icon name="arrow" /></a>
        <p class="setup-version">v{download.version} beta / Source install / Apache 2.0</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ol class="setup-steps">
      <li><span class="step-number">01</span><h3>Install the CLI.</h3><p>Extract the current source preview and install it in a Python virtual environment.</p></li>
      <li><span class="step-number">02</span><h3>Prepare a worker.</h3><p>Use the Kaggle notebook. Keep the same private key in Kaggle Secrets and your local <code>.env</code>.</p></li>
      <li><span class="step-number">03</span><h3>Connect and work.</h3><p>Use its fresh URL. Run from the source checkout; add <code>--workspace</code> to select your project.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <Command label="Connect your text worker" command={'freecompute --remote-url "PASTE-KAGGLE-URL-HERE"'} />
    <p class="reconnect-note">Tunnel changed? Enter <code>/connect PASTE-KAGGLE-URL-HERE</code>. It reuses your key for this run. Resolve active or uncertain requests first.</p>
  </div>
</section>
